```

Explanation:
To create an array of numbers from 1 to 10, we first allocate memory for an array of size 11 using `new Array(11)`. However, this will initialize all elements as `undefined`. To populate the array with numbers from 1 to 10, we use a `for` loop to assign each number to its corresponding index. The loop starts at index 0 and ends at index 10, so the last element in the array is assigned the value 11, which we don't need, so we can remove it later or leave it as it is depending on your use case. Finally, we log the array to the console to verify the result.

